{% extends "_research_base.md.j2" %}
{% block focus %}
Name concrete competitors and substitutes locally, regionally and online, with what they offer and charge. Include free and DIY substitutes and anyone who has closed.

Search strategy:
1. Count companies with `prh search --industry <TOL 2025 prefix> --municipality Rääkkylä`, then the neighbouring municipalities (Kitee, Liperi, Joensuu, Savonlinna); note how many are `Lakannut` (closed) and when. Once the rows show which 5-digit codes fit the idea (e.g. `55203` holiday cabins), compare the municipalities on that code.
2. Name the active ones: web searches for the service plus the place, Google Maps listings quoted on the web, marketplaces and booking platforms; fetch each competitor's own page for its offer and prices.
3. Check names you find with `prh search --name "<company>"` (still registered? since when?).
4. Substitutes: free public services, DIY, bigger players in Joensuu or online that deliver here.

Finnish search terms: `<palvelu> Rääkkylä`, `<palvelu> Pohjois-Karjala`, `<palvelu> Joensuu`, `yritys`, `palveluntarjoaja`, `lopettanut`, `konkurssi`, `ilmainen`, `tee se itse`.

Finnish data tools for this dimension: `prh` (company counts by industry and municipality, closed companies, name checks).
